INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(165700, 0, 1657, 0, 0, 0, 'Darnassus', 'Darnassus is the capital of the night elves, raised in the high boughs of the World Tree Teldrassil off the northern coast of Kalimdor. After the Battle of Mount Hyjal cost the kaldorei their immortality, druids led by Fandral Staghelm grew the tree, and the city took root in its branches as a monument to their people''s survival. Unlike the stone cities of men and dwarves, it lies open to the sky. Its halls stand far apart among groves and leafy paths, and a quiet lake at its heart is crossed by graceful bridges. Ancients and Sentinels keep watch, and a portal in the west carries travelers down to Rut''theran Village. High Priestess Tyrande Whisperwind rules from the Temple of the Moon, while Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm leads the druids from the Cenarion Enclave, and the two do not always agree. The tree''s growth remains flawed, and a quarrel simmers between Darnassus and the druids of Moonglade.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darnassus (founding after the Third War, open to the sky, buildings set apart, central lake and bridges, portal from Rut''theran); quest 933 reward text (Malfurion never returned; Fandral convinced the Circle of Ancients); quest 935 description (dragons withheld blessing); npc_text 3018 (portal in the western section); quest 6761 and 6762 (tension with Moonglade); DB spawns: Ancient Protector 2041, Ancient of War 3469, Ancient of Lore 3468, Darnassus Sentinel 4262; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tyrande_Whisperwind (clashes with Fandral; sole leader of Darnassus with Malfurion gone)'),
(165701, 1, 1657, 1, 0, 0, 'Cenarion Enclave', 'In the northern reaches of Darnassus lies the Cenarion Enclave, home of the city''s druids. Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm holds court in the great tree at its heart, and his second, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, trains young druids on the level below and answers the callers the Arch Druid would rather not see. Hunters learn their craft here from Jocaste and Dorion, while in a quieter corner the rogue trainers Syurna and Erion Shadewhisper keep to the shadows. Lelanai tends the nightsabers the Sentinel army has long relied upon, offering them only to proven friends of Darnassus. Behind the Arch Druid''s tree, Jenal the ditch digger guards heaps of Un''Goro soil, and Rellian Greenspyre walks the pathways deep in thought.', 'zone_areas: Fandral 3516, Mathrengyl 4217, Jocaste 4146, Dorion 4205, Syurna 4163, Erion 4214, Lelanai 4730, Jenal 9047, Rellian 3517 all in area 1658; npc_text 3024 (druids in the northern section); quest 3781 description (Mathrengyl downstairs); quest 6761 description (Mathrengyl as his second); npc_text 3942, 5844 (Lelanai: nightsabers, Sentinel army, exalted only); quest 3764 description (Jenal behind this tree, piles of dirt); quest 922 description (Rellian walks the pathways)'),
(165702, 1, 1657, 2, 0, 0, 'Craftsmen''s Terrace', 'The Craftsmen''s Terrace, in the northeast of Darnassus, gathers the city''s artisans: alchemists, enchanters, tailors, leatherworkers, skinners and cooks, heirs to a millennium of knowledge. Young adventurers keep them busy with constant orders for supplies. Innkeeper Saelienne bids the weary rest beneath her roof and let Elune guide their dreams, and Lysheana charters new guilds. Envoys of the Argent Dawn keep a post here, gathering rumors that the Twilight''s Hammer and the naga have joined forces in Blackfathom Deeps, once a night elf temple with a powerful moonwell. A small library holds histories of the War of the Ancients, the World Tree and the Emerald Dream, and the Old Gods.', 'zone_areas area 1659: profession trainers, Innkeeper Saelienne 6735, Lysheana 4161, Dawnwatcher Shaedlass 4786, Argent Guard Manados 4784, Ancient of Lore 3468, books 175727, 175730, 175725; npc_text 3019, 3040 (northeastern section); npc_text 3034 (millennium of knowledge); quest 1582 description (craftsmen busy supplying young adventurers); npc_text 824 (Saelienne); quest 1198 and 1199 descriptions and request text (Twilight''s Hammer and naga, BFD a night elf temple with a powerful moonwell); quest 1198 description (rumors of the union of the Twilight''s Hammer and the naga)'),
(165703, 1, 1657, 3, 0, 0, 'Warrior''s Terrace', 'The Warrior''s Terrace spreads inside the city''s gate, where an Ancient of War stands guard and Sentinels keep watch. Arias''ta and Darnath Bladesinger teach the warrior''s art, and Elanaria tests the most promising before taking them as pupils. The smith Mathiel works elunite, a metal blessed by Elune herself, and Ilyenia Moonfire teaches the bow, the staff and other weapons. Thyn''tel Bladeweaver, a commander of the Sentinels, keeps her post here. Battlemasters gather volunteers for Warsong Gulch, Arathi Basin and Alterac Valley.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darnassus (Warrior''s Terrace includes the city gate, forge, training dummies); zone_areas area 1660: Ancient of War 3469, training dummies, Arias''ta 4087, Darnath 7315, Elanaria 4088, Mathiel 6142, Ilyenia Moonfire 11866, Thyn''tel 8026, battlemasters, Arcanist Dulial 35599; quest 1692 reward text (elunite blessed by Elune); npc_text 10748, 10757 (Ilyenia teaches bows, staves, more); quest 1037 description (Thyn''tel a commander of the Sentinels)'),
(165704, 1, 1657, 4, 0, 0, 'Tradesmen''s Terrace', 'South of the Warrior''s Terrace lies the Tradesmen''s Terrace, the market of Darnassus. Its auctioneers take bids from across the Alliance, and its merchants sell blades, bows, staves, robes, mail and much else, while Talaelar offers the catch of the lake. The fishermen of Teldrassil moved here when attacks made Lake Al''Ameth unsafe, and Astaia teaches the angler''s craft by the water. Among these homes lives Treshala Fallowbrook, whose husband went far away into the Barrens. In a locked chest the Sentinels keep the belongings of the priestess Velinde Starsong, who vanished from her post in Ashenvale, and a copy of The Betrayer Ascendant, telling how Illidan turned to demonic power after his release, waits for any reader.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darnassus (Tradesmen''s Terrace south of Warrior''s Terrace, auction house); zone_areas area 1662: auctioneers, merchants 4171-4240, Talaelar 4221, Astaia 4156, Treshala 4521, Velinde''s Locker 19877, book 175759; npc_text 4333 (fishermen moved to Darnassus after attacks around Lake Al''Ameth); quest 1142 (Treshala); quest 1037, 1038 (Velinde, chest of her things)'),
(165705, 1, 1657, 5, 0, 0, 'The Temple Gardens', 'West of the Warrior''s Terrace, across a causeway, lie the Temple Gardens, where Sentinels stand watch along every path. Firodren Mooncaller teaches herbalism among the flower beds, and Herald Moonstalker cries the latest news from both continents, from calls to arms in the Plaguelands to the frontiers of Kalimdor. Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker of the Explorers'' League keeps his post here. Beyond the gardens to the west, a portal carries travelers down to Rut''theran Village. To the south a further causeway leads to the Temple of the Moon, the heart of the night elves'' faith.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darnassus (Temple Gardens west over a causeway from Warrior''s Terrace; Temple of the Moon south over a causeway); zone_areas area 1661: Darnassus Sentinel 4262 x16, Firodren 4204, Chardryn 4216, Herald Moonstalker 10878, Greywhisker 2912, Portal to Blasted Lands 195141; npc_text 6957 (Herald: news from both continents); quests 5091, 1047 (Herald''s notices); npc_text 3039 (herbalism in the Temple Gardens); quest 6344 (portal west of the Temple Gardens)'),
(165706, 1, 1657, 6, 1, 0, 'Temple of the Moon', 'The Temple of the Moon is the seat of the Sisters of Elune and the true center of power in Darnassus. At its heart a statue rises from a moonwell, its holy waters said to purify and cleanse corruption. Tyrande Whisperwind keeps her quarters on the upper level. Priestesses such as Astarii Starseeker, Jandria and Alathea teach those who follow Elune, while the scholar Gracina Spiritmight studies the threats rising in the south. Visitors are greeted with Elune''s blessing, and the temple''s teachers offer their wisdom and knowledge to those who seek it.', 'WMOAreaTable: Temple of the Moon is WMO 1079 group 632 with AreaTable id 1657, so it has no reachable id of its own; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Temple_of_the_Moon (seat of the Sisterhood of Elune, de facto capital building, statue in a moonwell, Tyrande''s quarters); quest 2520 description (central fountain''s holy waters purify and cleanse); DB spawns near Tyrande: Astarii 4090, Jandria 4091, Priestess Alathea 11401, Gracina 7740, Emissary Valustraa 17105 (mage trainer), Rukua 35281 (paladin trainer), Mordent Evenshade 36479; quest 4493 description (Gracina, silithid); quest 2972 completion text (the temple welcomes those seeking the aid of the servants of the Light); npc_text 4437, 4438 (Astarii and Jandria: Elune be with you; my wisdom is yours, as is my knowledge)'),
(165707, 2, 1657, 1, 1, 0, 'Tyrande Whisperwind', 'Tyrande Whisperwind, High Priestess of Elune, rules Darnassus from the Temple of the Moon. Ten thousand years ago she stood against Queen Azshara in the War of the Ancients, and through the long ages while the druids slept she led the Sentinels in guarding the forests. In the Third War she woke Malfurion from his long slumber, freed Illidan from his prison against Malfurion''s wishes, and fought beside humans and orcs at Mount Hyjal against Archimonde. She often clashes with Fandral Staghelm, the Arch Druid who leads the druids. She greets seasoned heroes warmly and asks them to share their tales with the young.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tyrande_Whisperwind (War of the Ancients, Long Vigil, Third War, freeing Illidan, Hyjal, clashes with Fandral, sole leader with Malfurion gone); quest 2972 request and reward text (greeting, asks to share tales; Jer''kai her priestess); quest 1081 description (Stonetalon Sentinels send heroes to her); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tyrande_Whisperwind (woke Malfurion; Malfurion forbade freeing Illidan)'),
(165708, 2, 1657, 2, 1, 0, 'Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm', 'Fandral Staghelm is the Arch Druid of Darnassus. A thousand years ago he led the night elves against the Qiraji in Silithus, who named him Khar''sis, hand of the earth. Today he leads the druids of Darnassus, and after Hyjal he won the Circle of Ancients over and grew Teldrassil, hoping to win back his people''s lost immortality. Proud and short of patience, he scorns idle visitors and says it was he, not Moonglade, who led his people out of darkness.', 'creature_text 15183 (Geologist Larksbane: Khar''sis; no script says it in this core); page_text 2794-2797 (father and son, Southwind fell, arrogance snuffed out); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fandral_Staghelm (War of the Shifting Sands; archdruid after Malfurion; Teldrassil); quest 935 reward text (yoke); quest 940 reward text (work never completed, immortality never restored); npc_text 2285 (gossip); quest 6761 description (led us out of the darkness, not Moonglade)'),
(165709, 2, 1657, 3, 1, 0, 'Mathrengyl Bearwalker', 'Mathrengyl Bearwalker is the Arch Druid''s second and one of the druid trainers of the Cenarion Enclave, keeping to the level below Fandral Staghelm''s chamber. He welcomes young druids as brothers and sisters and reminds them that they are the preservers of the balance, now and forever, as Cenarius taught. He also sees to the business his master would rather not handle himself. When the call for help came from Moonglade, the Arch Druid handed it to him, and he hands out the seeds for the Arch Druid''s research and gathers what grows from them, asking only that Fandral not be disturbed with every batch.', 'npc_text 4786 (preservers of the balance as Cenarius taught); quest 6761 description and reward text; quest 6762 description; quest 3781 reward text, 3785 description, 3803 reward text (uncomfortable near morrowgrain); DB: Mathrengyl 4217 subname Druid Trainer, gossip menu 1403'),
(165710, 2, 1657, 4, 1, 0, 'Gracina Spiritmight', 'Gracina Spiritmight is a priestess of the Temple of the Moon and a scholar who has spent long years studying the creatures unique to Azeroth, a historian besides. She is an associate of Shandris Feathermoon''s Protectorate, and when strange insects are reported in the deserts of Tanaris or the forests of Feralas, it is to her that the reports are sent, in the hope that she can say what the threat is and, more importantly, how it might be stopped.', 'quest 162 description and reward text; quest 4267 description, request and reward text (priestess, Protectorate, Shandris); quest 4493 description; quest 4510 description (stronger presence elsewhere); quest 4508 request and reward text (Alliance, Darnassus leaders, Fandral)'),
(165711, 2, 1657, 5, 1, 0, 'Rellian Greenspyre', 'Rellian Greenspyre is a druid of Darnassus, more often found walking the pathways of the Cenarion Enclave than resting in its halls. He is a friend of the herbalist Denalan, who camps on the shore of Lake Al''Ameth to study the sickly timberlings of Teldrassil, and he took an early interest in that work, with ideas of his own. His hope was to grow a timberling from a seed, and so help his friend in the search for a cure.', 'quest 922 description and reward text; quest 923 description and reward text; quest 2498 description'),
(165712, 2, 1657, 6, 1, 0, 'Syurna', 'Syurna trains rogues in the Cenarion Enclave and has nothing to say to anyone outside her craft; her order, she says, is darkness and shadows, eternal and invisible. She has an admirer she never asked for. Jannok Breezesong, who trains rogues in Dolanaar, is hopelessly lovestruck with her. His home is full of her portraits, he goes days without eating or sleeping as he laments the love they might have had, and since she will not see him, he sends her flowers by any courier he can find.', 'npc_text 4793, 4794 (gossip); DB: Jannok Breezesong 3599 spawn 9790,943 = area 186 Dolanaar; quest 2241 description (Jannok)'),
(165713, 2, 1657, 7, 1, 0, 'Thyn''tel Bladeweaver', 'Thyn''tel Bladeweaver is one of the commanders of the Sentinels, keeping her post on the Warrior''s Terrace. Into her keeping came the belongings of Velinde Starsong, the priestess who held back the demons of Felwood from Ashenvale until her efforts faltered little by little and one day she simply vanished. Velinde''s things, among them a journal of her duties, lie locked in a chest, and Thyn''tel will not speak of the priestess''s departure to a stranger without good reason. The Sentinels believe Velinde had her own reasons for leaving and could return at any time, for she did much to earn their trust.', 'quest 1037 description and reward text; quest 1038 description; DB: Velinde''s Locker 19877 in area 1662'),
(165714, 2, 1657, 8, 1, 13, 'Archmage Mordent Evenshade', 'Archmage Mordent Evenshade is an envoy of the Highborne, the night elf sorcerers who have hidden for ages in the ruins of Eldre''Thalas and are now drawn out by a change on the wind. He has come to the Temple of the Moon to seek an accord with Tyrande Whisperwind, and he waits for his audience under the cold eye of Sentinel Stillbough, who reminds him that the kaldorei have not forgotten the War of the Ancients or the minds behind it. Mordent concedes that the lure of power is great and that mistakes were made. Still, he will not leave until he is heard, warning that the kaldorei may soon need the knowledge his people keep.', 'creature_text 36479 and 36481 (whole exchange); npc_text 14984 (gossip: Highborne returning to light); quest 14409 description and reward text (Daros Moonlance, ruins of Eldre''Thalas, change is coming)'),
(165715, 2, 1657, 9, 1, 0, 'Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker', 'Chief Archaeologist Greywhisker represents the Explorers'' League in Darnassus, keeping his post by the Temple Gardens. He is used to friends in the Alliance dismissing his work as a mere hobby, but he insists that recent discoveries in Khaz Modan prove a great and powerful force threatens all of Azeroth, from Lordaeron to Kalimdor. Of late, his own dig crew in Darkshore gives him cause to worry: they have not sent word in weeks.', 'quest 730 description; zone_areas: Greywhisker 2912 in area 1661'),
(165716, 2, 1657, 10, 1, 0, 'Treshala Fallowbrook', 'Treshala Fallowbrook keeps a quiet home among the houses of the Tradesmen''s Terrace, the market quarter of Darnassus, and she meets strangers at her door with polite surprise. Her husband, Heralath, went far from Teldrassil, across the sea to the Barrens and into Razorfen Kraul, the thorny warren where the quilboar make their home, a dangerous place even for the bravest of travelers.', 'quest 1142 completion text (what brings you to my home); DB: Heralath Fallowbrook 4510 starts 1142 in Razorfen Kraul; Treshala 4521 ends it, spawn in area 1662; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Razorfen_Kraul (quilboar warren of thorny vines in the Barrens)'),
(165717, 3, 1657, 1, 1, 0, 'The Arch Druid''s Research', 'Innkeepers in the cities of the Alliance pass on a quiet request: the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus needs seasoned helpers for a vital research project, and none other than Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is leading it. The Arch Druid explains it once and will not repeat himself, warning that those who think such errands beneath them will not win his favor. The soil of Un''Goro Crater is rumored to hold potent magic, and he means to separate fact from falsehood. Twenty loads are wanted from each helper, unloaded behind his tree for Jenal the ditch digger, who mutters that conspirators would keep a visionary like him shackled to obscurity.', 'quests 3763, 3789, 3790, 10520 (innkeepers 6735, 6740, 5111, 16739); quest 3763 reward text; quest 3764 description, request and reward text; npc_text 2313 (Jenal); quest 3781 description and reward text; quest 3785 description and reward text; quest 3803 request and reward text; quest 3803 reward text (how the Arch Druid tolerates so much morrowgrain)'),
(165718, 3, 1657, 2, 1, 0, 'The New Frontier', 'Heralds in Darnassus, Stormwind and Ironforge cry a summons: the Cenarion Circle seeks honorable proxies to explore a forbidden wasteland far west of Tanaris, and all who would answer should see Fandral Staghelm. Those who do are met with scorn. The Arch Druid asks why the welfare of all Teldrassil should wait on the hunt for some bauble, and calls the druids of Moonglade fools who waste his time. He hands the matter to his second, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, with a warning offered as friendly advice: it was he, not the Circle in Moonglade, who led their people out of darkness when all was lost, and Teldrassil gives them new life. To believe otherwise is to swallow propaganda.', 'quests 1047, 1015, 1019 description and reward text (heralds 10878, 2198, 10877); quest 6761 description and reward text; quest 6762 description and reward text'),
(165719, 3, 1657, 3, 1, 0, 'Lady Sathrah', 'Sister Aquinne, a novice of the temple, seeks help for a once great creature of the forest, and sends those who answer to Priestess A''moora in the Temple of the Moon. A''moora tells of Lady Sathrah, a spider beloved of Elune. Graceful and pure, she spun silver threads through the moonlight to catch the evening mist, and the silvery dew she gathered had strong healing powers and was kept in the temple. But of late Sathrah has fallen into madness on the northern borders of Teldrassil near Wellspring Lake, and even her future young are threatened. The priestess regrets what she must ask: Sathrah is beyond hope, her suffering must be ended, and her silvery spinnerets brought back to the temple.', 'quest 2519 description; quest 2518 description, request and reward text; quest 2520 description and reward text; DB: Lady Sathrah 7319 spawns at 10980,1366 and 10994,1687 (northern Teldrassil)'),
(165720, 3, 1657, 4, 1, 0, 'Elanaria''s Trial', 'When a young warrior of Teldrassil shows promise, their teachers send them on to Elanaria on the Warrior''s Terrace of Darnassus, where their name already rings loudly. Before she will teach, she asks for proof of resolve. The satyr Vorlus Vilehoof has found one of the remote moonwells southeast of the Ban''ethil Barrow Den and splashes in its pure waters, defiling them with his filth, and only his horn will satisfy her. The path to the moonwell is well hidden, she warns, and only those who stay focused and alert will find it.', 'quest 1684 description and reward text (starters Kyra Windblade 3598, Moon Priestess Amara 2151); quest 1683 description and reward text; quest 1686 description and reward text; quest 1692 description and reward text; quest 1693 reward text; quests 1710, 1711');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(165702, 1, 13, 255, 'In recent days scribes have joined the craftsmen as well. Feyden Darkin teaches the new art of inscription, and Illianna Moonscribe sells the inks and parchment that its students need for their work.', 'DB: Feyden Darkin 30715 (Inscription trainer) and Illianna Moonscribe 30731 (Inscription supplies) in area 1659; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Inscription (added in patch 3.0.2 with Wrath of the Lich King)'),
(165703, 1, 8, 255, 'Since the Dark Portal opened, another battlemaster has joined them. Enlae calls fighters through to Outland, to the Eye of the Storm in Netherstorm, where Alliance and Horde struggle for its towers and the flag at its heart.', 'DB: Enlae 20383 <Eye of the Storm Battlemaster> in area 1660 (mod-individual-progression ipp_aware_npcs.sql: npc_ipp_tbc, shown from state 8); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Eye_of_the_Storm (Netherstorm, four towers and the flag)'),
(165703, 2, 13, 255, 'The war in Northrend reaches the terrace too. Battlemasters now send volunteers to the Strand of the Ancients and the Isle of Conquest, the battle mage Arcanist Dulial sends others north to the struggle for Wintergrasp, and training dummies stand ready for anyone eager to test a blade or a spell.', 'DB: Nivara Bladedancer 30580 <Strand of the Ancients Battlemaster>, Terrance Matterly 35023 <Isle of Conquest Battlemaster>, Landuen Moonclaw 34988, Arcanist Dulial 35599 <Wintergrasp Battle-Mage> in area 1660 (35023, 34988, 35599 are npc_ipp_wotlk in mod-individual-progression; 30580 is not phased, Strand of the Ancients came with patch 3.0.2); DB: Grandmaster''s, Expert''s, Master''s and Heroic Training Dummy 31144, 32666, 32667, 31146 in area 1660 (added with Wrath of the Lich King, as thunder_bluff.json 163805 part 2)'),
(165705, 1, 8, 255, 'Of late a mage''s portal shimmers in the gardens as well. It opens across the sea onto the Blasted Lands, close by the Dark Portal, and so speeds the Alliance''s travelers on the long road to Outland.', 'DB: Portal to Blasted Lands 195141 in area 1661; mod-individual-progression ipp_aware_npcs.sql: portals 195141/195142 use gobject_ipp_tbc, shown from state 8 (as orgrimmar.json 163706 and thunder_bluff.json 163804); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Portal_to_Blasted_Lands (portals in the capitals to the Blasted Lands near the Dark Portal)'),
(165706, 1, 8, 255, 'Since the draenei of the Exodar joined the Alliance, the temple has welcomed new friends. Emissary Valustraa, one of their number, teaches the arcane arts to young mages within its walls.', 'DB: Emissary Valustraa 17105 <Mage Trainer>, faction 1638 (Exodar), in the temple (not phased by mod-individual-progression; the draenei joined the Alliance in The Burning Crusade)'),
(165706, 2, 13, 255, 'Of late the temple holds other visitors too. Rukua, a draenei paladin, trains paladins here, and an envoy of the Highborne waits by the moonwell for an audience with the high priestess, admitting that this pale echo of the Well of Eternity still holds the same beauty and purity.', 'DB: Rukua 35281 <Paladin Trainer>; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Rukua (draenei paladin trainer in the Temple of the Moon, added in patch 3.2.0); DB: Archmage Mordent Evenshade 36479 (patch 3.3.0), creature_text 36479 group 9, said by smart_scripts actionlist 3647901'),
(165707, 1, 0, 255, 'Malfurion Stormrage is not at her side. After Hyjal he vanished, and to this day his people do not know what became of him. So Tyrande rules Darnassus alone, while Fandral Staghelm leads the druids in Malfurion''s place.', 'quest 933 reward text (Shan''do Stormrage never returned; no one knows what became of him; Fandral took over the druids); quest 935 (follows 929 and 933); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tyrande_Whisperwind (sole leader with Malfurion gone)'),
(165708, 1, 0, 255, 'The water of Teldrassil''s moonwells reaches him at last, poured into one vessel in Dolanaar after the long telling of the tree''s making: how Malfurion Stormrage vanished after Hyjal and never returned, and how the dragons Alexstrasza and Nozdormu refused their blessing, leaving its growth flawed. Fandral grumbles at the slow delivery and the choice of messenger. The weight of Teldrassil''s problems falls on his shoulders, he says, a yoke he wishes he could soon be rid of.', 'quest 935 description, completion and reward text; quests 929, 933, 7383 reward texts (the earlier steps of the chain)'),
(165708, 2, 0, 255, 'The Oracle Tree, which watches over Teldrassil''s growth, sends its reports to him, but none has come for a long while: its last runner was slain by harpies, and the tree has feared sending another. Once the harpies are driven from their nests and a greater calm spreads through the forest, the tree entrusts its message for the Arch Druid to the one who freed it, promising that the forest will see its bearer safely along its paths to the forest of stone.', 'quest 940 description (offered at the Oracle Glade after 937; the tree has feared sending another messenger); quest 937 description (the runner killed)'),
(165708, 3, 0, 255, 'Fandral reads the report and understands why the tree has kept silent for so long. Some of Teldrassil''s problems are lessened, he finds, while others grow into greater concerns, and he fears his work on the tree will never be completed, nor his people''s immortality restored.', 'quest 940 completion and reward text'),
(165709, 1, 0, 255, 'Mathrengyl apologizes for his master''s welcome to Moonglade''s volunteers. The air is thick with mistrust between the Arch Druid and Keeper Remulos, he admits, each suspecting the other of trickery, and the strange corruptions of Teldrassil that go on unabated do little to ease it. Yet duty to the Cenarion Circle remains, even if its leaders disagree, though he warns the tensions may grow.', 'quest 6761 reward text; quest 6762 description (offered on the 6761 turn-in)'),
(165709, 2, 0, 255, 'The morrowgrain troubles him more than he lets on. He takes the harvest ten at a time for the Arch Druid, but confesses that simply standing near the herb makes him uneasy, and he wonders how Fandral can bear to keep so much of it.', 'quest 3803 completion and reward text (auto-complete, so QUEST_DONE)'),
(165710, 1, 0, 255, 'Gracina knows the creatures at once. The night elves know this terror, she says: the insects are the silithid, and they will consume the land rapidly. They are no mere pests but the tools of one of the greatest threats that both Horde and Alliance will ever face.', 'quest 162 reward text; quest 4267 completion and reward text'),
(165710, 2, 0, 255, 'Her theory is that the silithid exist to devour everything in their path that is not of their kind, and that what has been seen so far is only the first stage. She suspects their strength comes from deeper in Kalimdor, from Un''Goro Crater, and sends word of it to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.', 'quest 4493 description'),
(165710, 3, 0, 255, 'Gracina doubts Pestlezugg''s report will do much good. She rails that the Alliance sees no enemy but the Horde and that even the city''s leaders cannot agree on the danger: Fandral Staghelm, she says, denies the silithid are the ancient threat she claims, and his ignorance is surpassed only by his arrogance. She now fears her guess about Un''Goro was wrong, and that a far stronger presence lies somewhere else.', 'quest 4508 completion and reward text; quest 4510 description (offered on the 4508 turn-in)'),
(165711, 1, 0, 255, 'A seed from the lake ended that hope. A corruption has grown in many of the timberlings, Rellian found, and seeds from such creatures carry their parents'' taint, beyond his talents to repair. Denalan, so skilled with growing things, may be the timberlings'' only hope. Until the source is found, those beyond help must be cut down, and the most tainted of all wander Wellspring Lake in northern Teldrassil.', 'quest 922 reward text; quest 923 description (offered on the 922 turn-in)'),
(165711, 2, 0, 255, 'The mossy tumors cut from the timberlings of Wellspring Lake are brought to him to be burned. They are the symptom of the timberlings'' disease, he says, and they are filled with a poison that must be cleansed from the new land.', 'quest 923 reward text'),
(165711, 3, 0, 255, 'Then word reached him from the lake: Denalan had discovered what may be causing the tumors that plague the timberlings. Rellian wasted no time, and sent help to his friend at once with a plea for haste, for Denalan needed their aid.', 'quest 2498 description'),
(165712, 1, 0, 255, 'Had she kept every flower that dolt sent her, Syurna remarks, she could have opened a shop. His gifts mean nothing to her, but his latest courier may prove useful, and she has work in mind for those of her craft.', 'quest 2241 reward text'),
(165712, 2, 0, 255, 'Her order wants to know what is happening to the forests of Teldrassil, and one being may know: Sethir the Ancient, a satyr hiding on a branch at the edge of the Oracle Glade. All who approached him, by force or diplomacy, met their doom, so she asks a young rogue to try stealth instead and learn what he carries in his packs.', 'quest 2242 description'),
(165712, 3, 0, 255, 'From Sethir''s packs comes a journal written in a tongue its bearer cannot read, but Syurna draws grim news from it. The sickness that has gripped the forests and rivers of Darkshore, she says, has begun to taint Teldrassil itself. There is nothing more her helper can do there, and she rewards the service with a blade.', 'quest 2242 reward text; item 7737 Sethir''s Journal (written in a language you cannot decipher)'),
(165714, 1, 0, 255, 'A journal from his colleague Daros Moonlance, who studies the city of Dalaran, finds its way to him. Mordent welcomes it: Daros was always meticulous in tracking their progress, and his words may help explain how far the Highborne have come. Perhaps, Mordent says, they will be seen more often once it is understood that they mean no harm.', 'quest 14409 description and reward text'),
(165716, 1, 0, 255, 'Heralath never came home. Mortally wounded in the warren, he sent the dwarf Lonebrow to carry a warning to Falfindel, and with his last strength begged that Treshala''s pendant of bonding, stolen by one of his attackers, be found and returned to her with word of his lonely death. When it reached her, she cried out that it was not fair. Sending the bearer away so that she might mourn alone, she swore that Heralath''s work would not die with him.', 'quest 1142 description and reward text'),
(165717, 1, 0, 255, 'The soil has a purpose. Fed with it in an evergreen pouch, costly Tharlendris seeds blossom into a scatter of potent herbs, and among them is morrowgrain, a mysterious herb about which little is known and which Fandral means to unravel. His second, Mathrengyl Bearwalker, sells the seeds in the enclave below.', 'quest 3781 description and reward text'),
(165717, 2, 0, 255, 'Mathrengyl takes in the harvest for the Arch Druid''s research and asks that Fandral not be disturbed each time a batch comes in. The need for morrowgrain, he says, is constant for now, and the mysterious properties of Un''Goro Crater grow clearer with each passing day.', 'quest 3785 description, completion and reward text'),
(165717, 3, 0, 255, 'Batch after batch goes to him, ten at a time. Mathrengyl admits that simply standing near the herb makes him uneasy, and he wonders how the Arch Druid can bear so much of it. To what end it is gathered, Fandral does not say.', 'quest 3803 completion and reward text (auto-complete, so QUEST_DONE)'),
(165718, 1, 0, 255, 'Mathrengyl apologizes for the welcome. Mistrust runs thick between the Arch Druid and Keeper Remulos, he explains, each suspecting the other of trickery, but the Circle''s work must go on. He sends the volunteers to Remulos'' majordomo, Rabine Saturna, in Nighthaven, warning that the tensions between Darnassus and Moonglade may yet grow.', 'quest 6761 reward text; quest 6762 description (offered on the 6761 turn-in)'),
(165719, 1, 0, 255, 'It is done, and the forest mourns Lady Sathrah, though A''moora holds that it had to be. The spinnerets are to be laid at the temple''s central fountain as an offering to Elune, whose holy waters purify and cleanse the corruption that drove the spider mad, so that the goddess may bless her and let her be reborn at peace.', 'quest 2518 completion and reward text; quest 2520 description (offered on the 2518 turn-in)'),
(165719, 2, 0, 255, 'The sacrifice is laid in the fountain. The loss of Lady Sathrah is distressing, A''moora says, but only in this way may she be reborn with a renewed spirit, and the priestess prays that Elune will willingly accept the offering.', 'quest 2520 reward text'),
(165720, 1, 0, 255, 'With Vorlus defeated and the moonwell cleansed, the training begins, and its next lesson is the forging of a warrior''s weapon. Long ago a ship broke on the rocks near the Auberdine lighthouse in Darkshore, scattering crates of elunite ore across the seabed, and its captain, the Shade of Elura, cursed herself to guard the cargo for all time. She must be defeated and the lost ore gathered.', 'quest 1683 reward text; quest 1686 description'),
(165720, 2, 0, 255, 'Elura''s defeat grants her a long deserved peace, and Elanaria places the gathered elunite in a case for the smith Mathiel, whose forge stands just to the south on the same terrace.', 'quest 1686 reward text; quest 1692 description'),
(165720, 3, 0, 255, 'Mathiel counts it an honor to work elunite, a metal blessed by the goddess Elune herself, and he sets to work at once shaping weapons from the ore for the pupil to choose among. Working it, he says, is both an honor and a pleasure.', 'quest 1692 reward text; quest 1693 reward text (auto-complete, so QUEST_DONE)'),
(165720, 4, 0, 255, 'In time Mathiel has other work for seasoned warriors. His colleague Furen Longbeard has made a discovery he is eager to test, and he seeks the sunscorched egg shells of the wyverns of Highperch in Thousand Needles, to render into a lacquer for the links of a new mail armor.', 'quest 1710 description and completion text');
